WindowPane visual README

Status: DONE
Milestone: Screenshot-rich product guide with actual native demo GIFs
Dependencies: 04_QUALIFICATION.todo
Purpose: Explain the preview visually without exposing private application data.

Tasks:
- [x] Export native live, opacity, keyed and aspect-fit sequences from the fixture.
- [x] Create and inspect compact GIFs and screenshots with explicit provenance.
- [x] Expand README setup, walkthrough, controls, recovery and preview limits.
- [x] Reconcile media reproduction notes, index, ledger and owned context.

Acceptance criteria:
- All images use the owned fixture or WindowPane controls; no private capture.
- GIFs show actual exported states, not fabricated UI interaction or timing.
- Media is linked locally, captioned and reproducible with documented tools.
- App behavior, fixture automation, human acceptance and publication stay distinct.

Completion evidence:
- Actual native --demo-assets export passed 27 checks. Standard CTest retained
  18 pure cases and 26 native checks. Both CTest targets pass in build\media.
- Four GIFs decode with 8/17/3/13 frames, expected timing and non-static output.
- Nine new PNG assets include three actual controls states, five pane cards
  and a four-state montage. Native surfaces and annotated derivatives are labeled.
- README includes 13 local images: four animations and nine PNGs.
- Full controls, representative native states, montage and encoded GIF samples
  visually reviewed; image decoding, local links and whitespace checked.
- No private screen capture, user-process termination, commit or publication.

Completion log:
- 2026-11-06: User requested proper README details and many GIFs/screenshots.
- 2026-11-06: Existing running preview locked its executable; built the harness
  in build\media instead of interrupting it. Initial extended teardown stalled;
  release capture before destroying the owned fixture fixed the export.
- 2026-11-06: Added reproducible native demo export and Pillow encoder. README
  now teaches setup, selection, live updates, opacity/keying, sizing, recovery,
